{% comment %}
  Upcoming events. The buy point of the seminars page.

  TWO SOURCES: a collection (one row per product, read from metafields), or
  hand-authored blocks when none is set. Blocks are the fallback because a
  typed price does not follow the product it sits beside -- and a dead handle
  degrades to those typed values silently, which has happened here once.

  THE SETTING IS `events_collection`, NOT `collection`. That id collides with
  Liquid's global collection drop and reads back EMPTY, so the section falls
  through to blocks and renders plausible rows from the wrong source. Same for
  `product`, `cart` and `customer`.

  METAFIELDS, all on the product, all namespace `custom`:

    seminar_city       single line text  "Tampa"
    seminar_state      choice list       "Florida" -- 50 states plus DC
    seminar_start      date              2026-09-25
    seminar_end        date              2026-09-26
    seminar_focus      choice list       "Upper Body" -- optional, blank renders empty
    seminar_venue      single line text  "Example Gym Downtown"
    seminar_address    single line text  "100 Example Avenue" (street)
    seminar_map        url               the Google Maps link
    seminar_time_start date and time     only the TIME half is shown
    seminar_time_end   date and time     only the TIME half is shown

  The last six feed the detail panel and are ALL OPTIONAL -- an empty one
  renders nothing rather than a blank label, and a row with none of them still
  opens to its buy button.

  Address is single line, not multi-line: multi-line returns newlines that read
  as one run-on unless every consumer remembers newline_to_br.

  HOURS ARE TWO TIMESTAMPS, and only the time halves show. Shopify has no
  time-only type, so each carries a date duplicating seminar_start -- which on
  a two-day seminar would contradict the row, since the end time is on day two
  but the hours line describes both days.

  date_time has NO TIMEZONE: it renders in the store's, not the venue's. 9am
  entered shows as 9am everywhere, which is wanted -- but only because nothing
  converts it. Do not "fix" that.

  The displayed date is DERIVED from start and end, so nobody can mistype it.
  Same month collapses to "September 25 & 26"; different months render both.

  SORTING. Liquid cannot sort a collection by a metafield, so rows are ordered
  by building `YYYYMMDD~index` strings and sorting those -- zero-padded and
  fixed-width, so a lexical sort is chronological. The index rather than the
  handle avoids `all_products`, capped at 20 lookups a page. No start date
  sorts last on 99999999 rather than first on an empty key.

  PAST EVENTS DROP OFF by themselves, judged on the end date so a seminar is
  still listed on its first morning.

  THE PRODUCT PAGE IS NO LONGER IN THE JOURNEY. A row used to be one big <a>,
  and an <a> cannot hold a <form>, which left only the product page or
  /cart/{variant}:1 -- neither reaching checkout. The row is now a <details>,
  and a <summary> carries no such restriction, so the panel holds a real
  add-to-cart with return_to. The whole-row click target was worth trading once
  the click bought something: the four facts that page held.

  `link_mode` survives for the fallback blocks and for a row whose product is
  missing. It is no longer the main path.

  ELEMENT. The root is a <div>: `"tag": "section"` already wraps this.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign anchor = section.settings.anchor | handle
  assign events = section.settings.events_collection
  assign today = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0
-%}

<div class="suf-section" {% if anchor != blank %}id="{{ anchor }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="suf-wrap">
    <div class="suf-semlist">
      {%- if events != blank -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign keyed = ''
          for p in events.products
            assign starts = p.metafields.custom.seminar_start.value | date: '%Y%m%d'
            if starts == blank
              assign starts = '99999999'
            endif
            assign keyed = keyed | append: starts | append: '~' | append: forloop.index0 | append: ','
          endfor
          assign keys = keyed | split: ',' | sort
          assign shown = 0
        -%}

        {%- for key in keys -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign idx = key | split: '~' | last | plus: 0
            assign product = events.products[idx]

            assign starts = product.metafields.custom.seminar_start.value
            assign ends = product.metafields.custom.seminar_end.value | default: starts

            # Judged on the end date, so a two-day seminar is still listed on
            # its first morning.
            #
            # `| plus: 0` on both sides is load-bearing: Liquid compares
            # strings with < by returning false, silently, so an unconverted
            # comparison never drops anything and the filter looks like it
            # works right up until a date passes.
            assign over = ends | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0
            assign is_past = false
            if ends != blank and over < today
              assign is_past = true
            endif
          -%}

          {%- if is_past == false and shown < section.settings.limit -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Captured OUTSIDE the liquid tag below, because a snippet cannot
              return a value -- render writes to output, so the only way to
              hold it is to capture what it prints.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- capture place -%}
              {%- render 'suf-seminar-place', product: product -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- assign place = place | strip -%}

            {%- liquid
              assign shown = shown | plus: 1

              # Each half is formatted on its OWN line. Chaining them --
              # `first | append: ' & ' | append: ends | date: '%-d'` -- pipes
              # the whole concatenated string into date, not the end date.
              assign m1 = starts | date: '%B'
              assign m2 = ends | date: '%B'
              assign first_half = starts | date: '%B %-d'
              if m1 == m2
                assign second_half = ends | date: '%-d'
              else
                assign second_half = ends | date: '%B %-d'
              endif
              assign when = first_half | append: ' & ' | append: second_half
              if starts == blank
                assign when = ''
              endif

              # `place` is captured below the liquid tag, from
              # snippets/suf-seminar-place.liquid, and falls back to the
              # product title when a seminar has neither city nor state.
              #
              # ONE LINE per statement inside a liquid tag: a continuation line
              # parses as its own statement and fails with a
              # LiquidHTMLSyntaxError, taking the section with it. And never
              # write a tag delimiter inside a `#` comment here -- it is not
              # lexed as a comment, so the delimiter closes the enclosing tag
              # and every statement after it renders to the page as text.
              assign city = place | default: product.title
              assign focus = product.metafields.custom.seminar_focus.value
              assign price = product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros

              assign sold_out = false
              unless product.available
                assign sold_out = true
              endunless

              # HOURS ARE TWO date_time METAFIELDS, joined here rather than in
              # the snippet, which takes resolved values only.
              #
              # Only the TIME half is displayed. The fields carry a full
              # timestamp because Shopify has no time-only metafield type, so
              # the date part duplicates seminar_start and would read as
              # a contradiction on a two-day seminar -- the end time is on day
              # two, but the hours line describes both days.
              #
              # %-l is unpadded 12-hour. %l pads to a leading space, which then
              # shows up as a gap after the en dash.
              assign t1 = product.metafields.custom.seminar_time_start.value
              assign t2 = product.metafields.custom.seminar_time_end.value
              #
              # EACH HALF FORMATTED ON ITS OWN LINE, for the third time in this
              # file. `hours | append: ' – ' | append: t2 | date: ...` pipes the
              # whole concatenated string into date, not the end time -- and it
              # does not error, it just renders something plausible and wrong.
              assign hours = ''
              if t1 != blank
                assign from = t1 | date: '%-l:%M %p'
                assign hours = from
                if t2 != blank
                  assign until = t2 | date: '%-l:%M %p'
                  assign hours = from | append: ' – ' | append: until
                endif
              endif

              # The street alone is not an address. seminar_address holds
              # "100 Example Avenue", which is unusable without the city
              # -- so the panel line is assembled here rather than asking the
              # merchant to type the city twice and keep the two in step.
              assign street = product.metafields.custom.seminar_address.value
              assign where = street
              if street != blank and city != blank
                assign where = street | append: ', ' | append: city
              endif

              if section.settings.link_mode == 'cart'
                assign vid = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id
                assign target = '/cart/' | append: vid | append: ':1'
              else
                assign target = product.url
              endif
            -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Every argument is a plain variable. A render argument takes a
              value, not an expression -- `sold_out: product.available == false`
              is a parse error, and the section 500s rather than degrading.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- render 'suf-semrow',
              city: city,
              date: when,
              focus: focus,
              price: price,
              target: target,
              sold_out: sold_out,
              cue: section.settings.cue,
              product: product,
              venue: product.metafields.custom.seminar_venue.value,
              address: where,
              map: product.metafields.custom.seminar_map.value,
              time: hours
            -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

      {%- else -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign product = block.settings.product
            assign target = block.settings.url
            if target == blank and product != blank
              if block.settings.link_mode == 'cart'
                assign vid = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id
                assign target = '/cart/' | append: vid | append: ':1'
              else
                assign target = product.url
              endif
            endif

            assign sold_out = false
            if product != blank
              assign price = product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros
              unless product.available
                assign sold_out = true
              endunless
            else
              assign price = block.settings.price
            endif
          -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            No metafields on the fallback branch. A hand-authored block has no
            product to read them from, and typing a venue and address into
            theme settings is the same lie the typed price already is -- it
            sits next to a real event and does not follow it. A block row shows
            what it can and links out.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- render 'suf-semrow',
            city: block.settings.city,
            date: block.settings.date,
            focus: block.settings.focus,
            price: price,
            target: target,
            sold_out: sold_out,
            cue: block.settings.cue,
            attrs: block.shopify_attributes
          -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.note != blank -%}
      <div class="suf-semnote">{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.note %}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Event list (SUF)",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 20,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "anchor",
      "label": "Anchor id",
      "info": "Lets a button elsewhere link here, e.g. \"upcoming\"."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Source" },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "events_collection",
      "label": "Seminars collection",
      "info": "Set this and the rows come from its products. City, dates and focus are read from each product's metafields; the Event blocks below are then ignored."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "limit",
      "label": "Rows to show",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "link_mode",
      "label": "Fallback link",
      "info": "Only used when a row cannot sell in place -- a missing or unavailable product. A normal collection row now opens a panel and buys from there, straight to checkout.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "product", "label": "Product page" },
        { "value": "cart", "label": "Add to cart, then cart" }
      ],
      "default": "product"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cue",
      "label": "Buy button text",
      "info": "Labels the button inside the open panel. The row's own control always reads \"Details\", because it opens rather than buys.",
      "default": "Reserve"
    },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "note", "label": "Note under the list" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "event",
      "name": "Event (fallback)",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "city", "label": "City" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "date", "label": "Date" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "focus",
          "label": "Focus",
          "info": "e.g. \"Upper Body\". Leave blank if not announced yet."
        },
        {
          "type": "product",
          "id": "product",
          "label": "Product",
          "info": "Supplies the price, the link and sold-out state."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "link_mode",
          "label": "Where Reserve goes",
          "options": [
            { "value": "product", "label": "Product page" },
            { "value": "cart", "label": "Add to cart, then cart" }
          ],
          "default": "product"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "price",
          "label": "Price fallback",
          "info": "Only used when no product is selected."
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "url", "label": "Link override" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "cue", "label": "Link text", "default": "Reserve" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Event list (SUF)",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "event" }, { "type": "event" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
